  "finish": {
    "requirements": [
      {
        "requirement": "Planter of four cells",
        "status": "met",
        "evidence": "The bases piece:0,0,0, 1,0,0, 2,0,0 and 3,0,0 are joined by joint bolts jointBolt:0#0,0#0, 0#1,0#0 and 0#2,0#0. Each has a drained bin, bin:*~hex-bin-third-drain. The catch: these are third-depth trays (about 37 mm deep), so there's not much soil per cell. Full and half-depth bins would hit the pipe."
      },
      {
        "requirement": "Water pipe running through the bases",
        "status": "met",
        "evidence": "run:run-1 is set to irrigation mode at level 0. It enters (0,0) on edge 3 and passes through (1,0), (2,0) and (3,0). The mesh check is clear."
      },
      {
        "requirement": "Pipe feeds every cell",
        "status": "partial",
        "evidence": "The pipe passes under all four cells, so it can reach each one. But the catalog has no emitter or outlet part to fit per cell, so the actual water connection into each bin isn't modelled. You would need to add your own drippers or holes."
      }
    ],
    "summary": "Four full bases sit in a straight row from (0,0) to (3,0), tied together with three joint bolts. One water pipe, set to irrigation mode (run-1), enters through the west wall of (0,0) and runs sideways through all four bases. Each cell has a drained third-depth bin, which is the deepest bin that fits above a pipe running sideways through a cell. check_build shows no rule errors and the mesh check is clear. The only note is an info message that some faces could still take caps."
  },
